preConditionHook:
// A protective stop sized by the average bar range SO FAR TODAY. Brooks
// quotes it as "around the height of an average bar so far today, maybe 10 to
// 15 cents" -- the cents are stock-specific, the multiple is the portable
// form.
//
// The window is what makes this its own rule: session-relative and GROWING
// through the day, starting at one bar at the open and resetting at the next
// one. No setting of AtrTrailingStop's fixed rolling N reproduces that, and
// this is a fixed protective stop rather than a trailing one.
//
// It is a mean of high-low, not of true range, and NOT the
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling accumulator -- there is no seeding or
// length-change behaviour to mirror here, just a running sum.
//
// barsIn is at least 1 on every evaluated bar (the session-start branch sets
// it to 1, the other increments from 0), so the division is safe.
//
// Direction-agnostic: a stop distance in dollars is the same both sides, as
// in StopLoss and AtrProfitTarget. BigPointValue is the raw contract
// multiplier and is NOT currency-converted while OpenPositionProfit is --
// TradeStation's own inconsistency, preserved as AtrProfitTarget preserves it.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the twin's date > date[1],
// mirrored as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)). Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    barsIn = 1;
    rangeSum = high[0] - low[0];
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
    rangeSum = rangeSum + (high[0] - low[0]);
}
avgRange = rangeSum / barsIn;
